    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0240" n="219" xml:id="pg219"/>

                <head>86. Memorandum From Secretary of State Vance to President Carter<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d86-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-03-18">March 18, 1977</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Libya.]</p>
                <p>3. <hi rendition="#italic">Libyan Assassination Attempt:</hi> As you know, Phil
                    Habib called in the Libyan Ambassador to the UN Kikha on Wednesday to strongly
                    protest the fact that elements of the Libyan intelligence service in
                    collaboration with “Carlos” were plotting to assassinate our Ambassador to
                    Cairo, Herman Eilts.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d86-f2"/> Late this afternoon, the
                    Libyan Chargé in Washington came in to deliver his government’s denial of any
                    knowledge of the alleged operation against Eilts. I am enclosing a copy of the
                    Libyan note. You can see that the Libyan reply is unsatisfactory. [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">2 lines not declassified</hi>] I may authorize supplying
                    the Libyans with more specific details of the assassination operation. I will be
                    back in touch with you on this case.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d86-f3"/></p>
                <p>[Omitted here is material unrelated to Libya.]</p>


                <xi:include href="d86-a1.xml" xpointer="d86-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
